Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 03:44:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?P35:=20drc=5Fengine=20loadRules=20=E2=80=94=20r?=
 =?UTF-8?q?eserve=20+=20move-append=20instead=20of=20copy-push=5Fback?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Micro but clean: N-1 vector reallocs on a rules file with many rules
were happening because m_rules.push_back grew geometrically without a
reserve. Also the loop was pushing by copy — each push_back atomic-bumped
the shared_ptr refcount, then destroyed the source copy in the local
vector, atomic-decrementing it. Move-append avoids both atomics.

Trivial correctness: rules vector goes out of scope at the end of
loadRules, so std::move'ing out is fine.
---
 pcbnew/drc/drc_engine.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pcbnew/drc/drc_engine.cpp b/pcbnew/drc/drc_engine.cpp
index c0251fae..63e10f0f 100644
--- a/pcbnew/drc/drc_engine.cpp
+++ b/pcbnew/drc/drc_engine.cpp
@@ -705,8 +705,13 @@ void DRC_ENGINE::loadRules( const wxFileName& aPath )
         // Copy the rules into the member variable afterwards so that if Parse() throws then
         // the possibly malformed rules won't contaminate the current ruleset.
 
+        // Bulk-move: reserve once, then move each shared_ptr out of the
+        // local vector into m_rules. Saves N-1 vector reallocs on a
+        // rules file with many rules and avoids the atomic refcount
+        // bump that plain push_back(rule) does on a copy.
+        m_rules.reserve( m_rules.size() + rules.size() );
         for( std::shared_ptr<DRC_RULE>& rule : rules )
-            m_rules.push_back( rule );
+            m_rules.push_back( std::move( rule ) );
     }
 }
 
